14:["$","p","b417",{"children":["The real challenge for agencies today isn't ",["$","em","b413",{"children":["how do I talk to a chatbot?"]}]," but ",["$","em","b415",{"children":["how do I scale creative production without losing brand soul?"]}]," When you are prompting models one by one, you aren't being creative. You're being a data-entry clerk for an LLM. To move past this, we have to transition from being tool-operators to becoming system-architects."]}]
15:["$","h3","b419",{"children":["The system-architect paradigm"]}]
16:["$","p","b424",{"children":["The system-architect paradigm is the transition from manually manipulating individual model inputs to designing automated, interconnected workflows that carry a high-level goal from brief to finished assets. Instead of asking ",["$","em","b421",{"children":["what is the best prompt for this headline?"]}],", the system-architect asks ",["$","em","b423",{"children":["how do I build a pipeline that takes a 10-page brand strategy and turns it into 50 unique, on-brand assets?"]}]]}]
17:["$","h2","b426",{"id":"defining-the-brief-to-execution-framework","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Defining the Brief-to-Execution framework"]}]
18:["$","p","b428",{"children":["The solution to prompting fatigue is a structured Brief-to-Execution framework. This methodology moves the generative AI workflow away from fragmented chats and into a unified production line, where agents handle the volume and humans handle the vision."]}]
19:["$","p","b430",{"children":["By establishing a singular master brief as the source of truth, the framework ensures that every output, whether copy, visual assets, or video, derives from the same strategic intent rather than isolated, manual prompts. This shifts the human role from manual execution to orchestration, allowing for a cohesive multi-channel campaign where every output, from a social post to a video script, maintains brand alignment because it draws on the same brief and the same brand context. This centralized approach eliminates the drift that occurs when individual designers or writers prompt AI models independently, keeping the final execution close to the original strategy."]}]
1a:["$","p","b432",{"children":["The framework consists of three distinct phases."]}]
1b:["$","ol","b435-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b435",{"children":[["$","strong","b433",{"children":["Strategic intent (human). "]}],"The human defines the why and the who. This is the master brief containing brand voice, audience personas, and campaign goals."]}],["$","li","b438",{"children":[["$","strong","b436",{"children":["Agent orchestration (Melius). "]}],"The brief is ingested into an orchestration layer like Melius, which breaks the high-level intent into actionable tasks and builds them out on a shared canvas."]}],["$","li","b441",{"children":[["$","strong","b439",{"children":["Refined output (human). "]}],"The agents produce the Labor of Execution, and the human returns to perform the final Labor of Taste, selecting and polishing the best versions."]}]]}]
1c:["$","h2","b443",{"id":"the-human-as-creative-director","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["The human as creative director"]}]
1d:["$","p","b449",{"children":["In this new workflow, the human role evolves into that of a creative director. A creative director doesn't necessarily pick up the brush; they set the constraints and judge the results. This shift is critical because it separates the ",["$","strong","b445",{"children":["Labor of Execution"]}]," from the ",["$","strong","b447",{"children":["Labor of Taste"]}],"."]}]
1e:["$","h3","b451",{"children":["The Labor of Execution, assigned to agents"]}]
1f:["$","p","b453",{"children":["Agents are far superior to humans at the repetitive, high-volume tasks that traditionally eat up agency hours."]}]
20:["$","ul","b456-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b456",{"children":[["$","strong","b454",{"children":["Variations. "]}],"Creating 20 different versions of a headline for A/B testing."]}],["$","li","b459",{"children":[["$","strong","b457",{"children":["Formatting. "]}],"Resizing a master visual for 15 different social-media aspect ratios."]}],["$","li","b465",{"children":[["$","strong","b460",{"children":["Contextualization. "]}],"Taking one campaign concept and building out the full set (the social cut, the email header, the video storyboard) all drawn from the same brief, or ",["$","$L3b","b463",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b462","href":"/blog/static-ad-from-style-reference","isNewTab":false},"children":["building a static ad from a style reference"]}]," so a new subject matches a look you already have."]}],["$","li","b468",{"children":[["$","strong","b466",{"children":["On-brand output. "]}],"Holding every asset to the same stored brand context (voice, palette, typography, reference imagery) instead of eyeballing a 50-page guidelines deck by hand."]}]]}]
21:["$","h3","b470",{"children":["The Labor of Taste, retained by humans"]}]
22:["$","p","b472",{"children":["This is where the value of the human creative lies. Agents cannot feel the vibe of a cultural moment or understand the nuance of irony and empathy."]}]
23:["$","ul","b475-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b475",{"children":[["$","strong","b473",{"children":["Setting the creative vision. "]}],"Deciding that a brand needs to feel nostalgic but futuristic rather than just modern."]}],["$","li","b478",{"children":[["$","strong","b476",{"children":["Defining constraints. "]}],"Setting the ethical boundaries and the never-go zones for the AI."]}],["$","li","b481",{"children":[["$","strong","b479",{"children":["Final quality gatekeeping. "]}],"The no or the yes. Looking at the 10 concepts generated by the agents and identifying the one that has the spark necessary for a successful campaign."]}]]}]
24:["$","h2","b483",{"id":"orchestrating-with-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Orchestrating with Melius"]}]
25:["$","p","b485",{"children":["Melius serves as the bridge between your strategic intent and the actual production of assets. It is the orchestration layer that prevents your workflow from devolving into a dozen browser tabs and disconnected conversations. When you use Melius, you aren't just sending a prompt to an AI; you are deploying a system-wide context."]}]
26:["$","ul","b488-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b488",{"children":[["$","strong","b486",{"children":["Brand context, stored once. "]}],"You give Melius your brand context, written instructions plus reference images, and Mel applies it to every prompt, node title, and output automatically, so the work starts on-brand instead of you restating the rules each time."]}],["$","li","b494",{"children":[["$","strong","b489",{"children":["The right model for each job. "]}],"A campaign spans copy, images, video, and audio, and no single model is best at all of them. Mel plans the work and routes each job to the best model across ",["$","$L3b","b492",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b491","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false},"children":["every major provider under one subscription"]}],", then lays the results out together on one canvas."]}],["$","li","b497",{"children":[["$","strong","b495",{"children":["One shared context. "]}],"Because every generation draws on the same brief and the same brand context on one canvas, the pieces stay coherent. If the brief calls for a dark, cinematic tone, the copy Mel writes and the images it generates pull from that same intent instead of drifting apart across separate chats."]}],["$","li","b500",{"children":[["$","strong","b498",{"children":["Steer in plain language. "]}],"Instead of rewriting prompts one at a time, you tell Mel what to change (make it more aggressive, warmer grade, tighter crop) and it reworks the affected pieces on the canvas for you."]}]]}]
27:["$","p","b502",{"children":["This level of orchestration is what allows a single creative director to manage the output of what would traditionally be a 10-person production team."]}]
28:["$","h2","b504",{"id":"future-proofing-the-agency-workflow","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Future-proofing the agency workflow"]}]
29:["$","p","b506",{"children":["The competitive advantage in the next five years will not belong to the agency that uses AI; it will belong to the agency that masters the Brief-to-Execution workflow. The benefits are measurable."]}]
2a:["$","ul","b509-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b509",{"children":[["$","strong","b507",{"children":["Speed. "]}],"Moving from brief to a full-funnel campaign in hours instead of weeks."]}],["$","li","b512",{"children":[["$","strong","b510",{"children":["Consistency. "]}],"Holding one brand context across thousands of assets, so the same intent shows up whether it's the first render or the ten-thousandth."]}],["$","li","b515",{"children":[["$","strong","b513",{"children":["Scale. "]}],"Handling 5x the client volume without a 5x increase in headcount or overhead."]}]]}]
2b:["$","p","b517",{"children":["We are moving away from the magic-box view of AI, where you type a prompt and hope for a miracle. We are entering the era of the agentic workforce, where tools like Melius let you stop being an operator and start being a director. Your value is no longer in your ability to use the tools; it's in your ability to lead the system."]}]
2c:["$","p","b522",{"children":["Move beyond the prompt. ",["$","$L3b","b520",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b519","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true},"children":["Start directing your workflow with Melius"]}],"."]}]
2d:["$","h2","b524",{"id":"frequently-asked-questions","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Frequently asked questions"]}]
2e:["$","div","b525",{"className":"faq-list my-10 flex flex-col divide-y divide-black/10 border-y border-black/10","children":[["$","details","0",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is the Brief-to-Execution workflow?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Brief-to-Execution is a structured way of running creative production where a single master brief becomes the source of truth for every asset. Instead of prompting AI models one by one, a human defines the strategy, an orchestration layer like Melius turns that intent into work on a shared canvas, routing each job to the right model and holding every output to one brand context, and the human returns to select and polish the best results. It moves the work from fragmented chats into one unified production line."}]]}],["$","details","1",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["How does the Brief-to-Execution framework solve inconsistency in AI creative work?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"By establishing a singular master brief as the source of truth, the framework ensures every output, whether copy, imagery, or video, derives from the same strategic intent rather than isolated prompts. This eliminates the drift that occurs when designers and writers prompt models independently, so a social post and a video script stay on-brand because they draw on the same brief and the same brand context."}]]}],["$","details","2",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is the difference between the Labor of Execution and the Labor of Taste?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"The Labor of Execution is the repetitive, high-volume work: generating copy variations, resizing a master visual for fifteen aspect ratios, keeping every asset against your brand context. Agents handle it. The Labor of Taste is judgment: setting the creative vision, defining the never-go zones, and picking the one concept with the spark. Humans keep it."}]]}],["$","details","3",{"className":"faq-item","children":["$L3c","$L3d"]}],"$L3e"]}]
2f:["$","section","related",{"className":"relative w-full pb-section bg-gray-background","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"color":"gray"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-300 px-5 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-h-2 mb-12 text-center text-balance text-gray-dark-1","children":"Related Articles"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto grid w-full max-w-max grid-cols-1 gap-11 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","$L3f","post-seedance-2-5-anticipation",{"post":{"_key":"post-seedance-2-5-anticipation","slug":"seedance-2-5-anticipation","category":"modus-news","title":"Seedance 2.5 is coming: ByteDance's next-gen AI video model","isoDate":"2026-07-07","date":"July 7, 2026","readTime":"6 Min Read","excerpt":"Seedance is behind more than a quarter of every video generation on Melius, and its share keeps climbing. ByteDance's Seedance 2.5 is announced with 50 reference inputs, synced audio, and, per its makers, native 4K. Here is the real usage data behind Seedance today, and an honest read on what 2.5 does and does not confirm.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/seedance-2-5/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is Seedance 2.5?","answer":"Seedance 2.5 is ByteDance's next-generation AI video model, announced on June 23, 2026. Per ByteDance, it generates clips up to 30 seconds long, accepts up to 50 multimodal reference inputs, and co-processes audio in the same latent space as the video so sound and action stay in sync. It has not been publicly released, so these are announced specifications rather than independently tested numbers."},{"question":"When is Seedance 2.5 coming out?","answer":"It is in global enterprise beta now, with public access rolling out in early July 2026. We route across every major model at Melius, so we will add Seedance 2.5 as soon as public access opens."},{"question":"What is new in Seedance 2.5 compared to Seedance 2.0?","answer":"The clearest change is reference capacity, up from 12 inputs to 50, covering images, audio, 3D white models, and style references. ByteDance also describes native audio synchronisation, local region editing, longer clips, and around 20% better prompt adherence. Native 4K with 10-bit color is reported too, though the 4K upgrade shown at the same event was attributed mainly to a Seedance 2.0 tier, and ByteDance has not published a separate resolution spec for 2.5, so treat 4K as an announced feature rather than a confirmed one."},{"question":"How much is Seedance used on Melius?","answer":"A lot. Seedance makes up 26.7% of all video generations on Melius, one of the two most-used video models on the platform, and about 4,400 teams have run it. Its share has climbed from 6.5% in March 2026 to nearly 30% today."},{"question":"How do you use Seedance 2.0?","answer":"You can use Seedance 2.0 on Melius today. Pick Seedance in the video model picker, give it a text prompt or, for production work, a reference image to animate, and run it. Because every model shares one credit pool, you can compare the same shot across Seedance, Kling and Veo side by side without juggling separate budgets."},{"question":"Is Seedance free to use?","answer":"Seedance runs on paid generation credits like every frontier video model. On Melius those credits are shared across every image, video and audio model in one pool, so you are not buying a separate Seedance subscription to try it."},{"question":"Will Seedance 2.5 be available on Melius?","answer":"It already is. Seedance 2.5 shipped and is in the Melius video model picker alongside Kling, Veo, Sora, and Wan, with 30-second clips, generated audio, and up to 50 reference files."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"see-it-for-yourself","title":"See It"},{"_key":"a-quarter-of-every-video-and-climbing","title":"The Numbers"},{"_key":"what-ai-video-generation-models-struggle-at","title":"The Hard Part"},{"_key":"get-ready-for-it","title":"Get Ready"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b157","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b154","text":"Right now, over a quarter of video generation traffic on Melius is routed to Seedance 2.0. Initially, Seedance wasn't heavily used, and didn't even cover a tenth of our generations in regards to videos. It just quietly became one of the models people here reach for when they need a quality video to post, and its share has climbed nearly every month since our inception in spring. When ByteDance announced ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b155","text":"Seedance 2.5","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b156","text":", it was not one more model to go and evaluate. It's an upgrade to something a lot of users are already excited about and are still pushing the boundaries of.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b159","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b158","text":"This piece is two things: what our own generation data says about how people use Seedance right now, and a read on what 2.5 promises. The usage numbers here are ours, and they are pulled directly from our data. Seedance 2.5 is not public yet, so its specs are based on what info ByteDance has released on it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b161","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b160","text":"See it for yourself","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"see-it-for-yourself"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b163","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b162","text":"Start with the output, because that is what earns the usage. These are real Seedance 2.0 generations from Melius, one model across four different jobs: a product beauty shot, a character moment, a cinematic frame, and a scene with a lot of motion. Not a cherry-picked hero reel, just the kind of work people run through it every day.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"videoCompare","_key":"b164","caption":"Real Seedance 2.0 output on Melius, the same model across four different jobs. ByteDance says 2.5 extends work like this to 30-second clips with synced audio and higher resolution.","clips":[{"label":"Product","src":"/videos/blog/seedance-2-5/seedance-product.mp4","poster":"/images/hero/hero-1.webp","aspectRatio":"16 / 9"},{"label":"Character","src":"/videos/blog/seedance-2-5/seedance-character.mp4","poster":"/images/hero/hero-2.webp","aspectRatio":"16 / 9"},{"label":"Cinematic","src":"/videos/blog/seedance-2-5/seedance-cinematic.mp4","poster":"/images/hero/hero-3.webp","aspectRatio":"16 / 9"},{"label":"Motion","src":"/videos/blog/seedance-2-5/seedance-motion.mp4","poster":"/images/hero/hero-4.webp","aspectRatio":"16 / 9"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b166","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b165","text":"A quarter of every video, and climbing","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"a-quarter-of-every-video-and-climbing"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b170","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b167","text":"Seedance is not something people just experiment with and forget on the platform. It is behind ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b168","text":"26.7% of every video generation on Melius","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b169","text":", one of only two models that carry the bulk of video work here, and around 4,400 teams have used it. Last week its share sat near 30%. What makes that striking is how fast it happened.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"lineChart","_key":"b171","title":"The rise of Seedance on Melius","caption":"Seedance's share of finished video jobs on Melius. From low usage in March to more than a quarter of all video work, Seedance has become one of the most-used video models on our platform.","unit":"%","yMax":30,"points":[{"label":"March","value":1},{"label":"April","value":10},{"label":"May","value":22},{"label":"June","value":30}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b173","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b172","text":"That entire climb ran on Seedance 2.0 alone. Nobody was pushed onto it or was even the model that we automatically routed to. People tried it against everything else we offer, side by side, and kept coming back. That is the useful signal, and it is why a generational update matters more here than a version number usually would.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b178","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b175","href":"/blog/nano-banana-image-models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b174","text":"There is a tell in how they use it. In our data, where we can see the mode, image-to-video beats text-to-video by more than a 2:1 ratio. This is the proof that Seedance is used for production quality videos, not just novelty prompting. People are not prompting Seedance with â€œcat astronautâ€ to see what happens. They are bringing a frame they already validated, a product, a character, a locked composition they love, and asking the model to move it and use it as a reference without breaking it. That starting frame is usually generated in an image model first, which is why picking the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b176","text":"right Nano Banana model","marks":["b175"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b177","text":" for the still feeds directly into a better clip.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b180","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b179","text":"What AI video generation models struggle at","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-ai-video-generation-models-struggle-at"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b182","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b181","text":"A clip that looks good for three seconds is a solved problem. Most modern models clear that bar. The hard part, the part that decides whether AI video is a toy or a tool, is everything after those three seconds: holding a face across a shot, keeping a product on-model, running long enough to be usable, carrying its own sound, and not forcing you to throw away a great take because one detail came out wrong.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b184","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b183","text":"Read the Seedance 2.5 feature list with that in mind and it stops looking like a spec dump. Every headline item is aimed at exactly those production problems. One caveat before the list: Seedance 2.5 is not public yet, so what follows is ByteDance's announcement, not a benchmark.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b187","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b185","text":"Up to 50 reference inputs, from 12. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b186","text":"Four times the old ceiling, spanning images, audio, 3D white models, and style guides. That is what it takes to hold a character or a brand steady across a longer shot instead of watching it drift frame by frame.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b190","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b188","text":"Native audio, in one pass. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b189","text":"Audio and video are generated together, in the same latent space, so sound is matched to the action rather than dubbed on afterward. This is the feature people already fake today with a separate audio step.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b193","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b191","text":"Local editing. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b192","text":"Fix one region of a clip without regenerating the whole thing, so a single wrong detail no longer costs you the take you liked. At 30 seconds a clip, that is the difference between an edit and a reroll.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b196","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b194","text":"Longer clips. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b195","text":"Up to 30 seconds in a single generation, with a beta mode reaching three minutes. Long enough to be a finished shot, not a loop.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b197","rows":[{"_key":"b198","cells":[{"_key":"b199","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b201","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b200","text":"Capability","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b202","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b204","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b203","text":"Seedance 2.5 (as announced)","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b205","cells":[{"_key":"b206","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b208","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b207","text":"Reference inputs","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b209","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b211","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b210","text":"Up to 50 multimodal inputs, up from 12","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b212","cells":[{"_key":"b213","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b215","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b214","text":"Audio","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b216","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b218","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b217","text":"Co-processed with video for native sound sync","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b219","cells":[{"_key":"b220","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b222","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b221","text":"Editing","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b223","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b225","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b224","text":"Local region edits without a full regeneration","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b226","cells":[{"_key":"b227","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b229","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b228","text":"Clip length","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b230","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b232","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b231","text":"Up to 30 seconds, with a beta mode reaching 3 minutes","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b233","cells":[{"_key":"b234","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b236","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b235","text":"Resolution","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b237","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b239","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b238","text":"4K capabilities, 10-bit color (claimed, disputed)","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b240","cells":[{"_key":"b241","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b243","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b242","text":"Prompt adherence","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b244","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b246","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b245","text":"Around 20% better, per ByteDance","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b247","cells":[{"_key":"b248","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b250","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b249","text":"Availability","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b251","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b253","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b252","text":"Enterprise beta now, public access in early July 2026","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b255","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b254","text":"The references jump and the audio change are the two most consistently reported, and the two that map most directly onto how people already work. ByteDance also reports 4K capabilities with 10-bit color and roughly 20% better prompt adherence, though the 4K figure is muddier than the rest, since the same event also gave Seedance 2.0 its own native 4K tier. It was announced June 23, 2026, and is to release soon.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b257","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b256","text":"Get ready for it","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"get-ready-for-it"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b259","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b258","text":"Seedance 2.5 joins the Melius video picker the moment public access opens. Three things set you up before it does.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b262","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b260","text":"Keep building with Seedance 2.0. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b261","text":"It is one of the strongest video models on the platform today, and everything you learn about prompting it carries straight over.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b265","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b263","text":"Gather your references. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b264","text":"If you have been rationing reference frames to fit the old limit, start collecting the full set now. 2.5 gives you room for up to 50.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b271","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b268","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b266","text":"Compare it against the field. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b267","text":"Run the same shot through Seedance, Kling, and Veo side by side. Because Melius puts ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b269","text":"every model under one subscription","marks":["b268"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b270","text":" and one credit pool, you can mass produce and compare videos without juggling separate budgets, so you get the best chance of landing the video you want.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b273","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b272","text":"If 2.5 delivers even most of what is on the sheet, it sharpens every reason people picked it in the first place.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b279","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b276","href":"/blog/seedance-2-5","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b274","text":"Update: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b275","text":"Seedance 2.5 has since shipped. See ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b277","text":"what Seedance 2.5 actually supports on Melius","marks":["b276"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b278","text":" for the released specs.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b284","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b281","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b280","text":"Want to see how your own generations break down by model? ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b282","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b281"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b283","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b286","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b285","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b287","items":"$2f:props:children:1:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:post:faq"}]}}],"$L40","$L41"]}]]}]]}]
