3c:["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What does an orchestration layer like Melius actually do?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}]
3d:["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"You store your brand context with Melius once, written instructions plus reference images, and Mel, its creative-director agent, applies it to every prompt, node title, and output automatically. Mel plans the work on a shared canvas and routes each job to the best model for it, so you steer in plain language instead of rewriting prompts one at a time."}]
3e:["$","details","4",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Why isn't one-shot prompting enough for agencies?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"One-shot prompting forces a human to act as a manual operator, micromanaging each output in isolation. It doesn't scale, and it produces drift because every prompt is disconnected from the last. Agencies that need volume without losing brand consistency have to move from operating tools to architecting systems."}]]}]
40:["$","$L3f","post-nano-banana-image-models",{"post":{"_key":"post-nano-banana-image-models","slug":"nano-banana-image-models","category":"modus-news","title":"Which Nano Banana model should you use?","isoDate":"2026-07-03","date":"July 3, 2026","readTime":"8 Min Read","excerpt":"Google's Nano Banana is three image models, not one. We pulled real generation data from Melius to work out when to use Nano Banana Pro, Nano Banana 2, and Nano Banana 2 Lite.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/nano-banana/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is Google Nano Banana?","answer":"Nano Banana is a family of three Google image models: Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image), Nano Banana 2 (Gemini 3.1 Flash Image), and Nano Banana 2 Lite (Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite Image). Each one trades speed for quality a little differently."},{"question":"What is the difference between Nano Banana Pro and Nano Banana 2?","answer":"Nano Banana Pro is a reasoning model. It is slower, but it keeps branding and characters consistent, renders readable text, and outputs native 4K. Nano Banana 2 is a faster mid-tier model that leans more cinematic and creative."},{"question":"Is Nano Banana 2 better than Nano Banana Pro?","answer":"It depends on the job. Nano Banana 2 is faster and scores higher in blind text-to-image voting, so it can look better at a glance. Nano Banana Pro wins the work that matters commercially: consistency across a set, readable text, native 4K, and following a full style guide. On Melius, Pro gets used about five times as much as Nano Banana 2, so the model people vote for is not the model they run."},{"question":"Can Nano Banana Pro make videos?","answer":"No. Every Nano Banana model, including Pro, is an image model. For video you route to a dedicated video model like Kling, Veo or Seedance. On Melius you can do both on one canvas: generate the still in Nano Banana Pro, then feed it straight into a video model."},{"question":"Which Nano Banana model is fastest?","answer":"Nano Banana 2 Lite. In our data it averages about 9 to 10 seconds, roughly three to four times faster than the other two. Reach for it when you are iterating quickly."},{"question":"Which Nano Banana model is best for text in images?","answer":"Nano Banana Pro. Its reasoning step is what lets it render readable text and hold a layout together, so commercial users lean on it for anything with words in the frame."},{"question":"Does a higher benchmark score mean a model is better for my work?","answer":"Not really. A blind single-image vote rewards whatever looks best at a glance. Real work rewards other things, like consistency across a set and readable text. That is why Pro gets the most real use even though its lighter siblings score higher on text-to-image boards."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"what-are-the-nano-banana-models","title":"The Models"},{"_key":"how-fast-is-each-model","title":"Speed"},{"_key":"what-do-people-actually-build-with-each","title":"What People Build"},{"_key":"how-do-they-score-on-benchmarks","title":"Benchmarks"},{"_key":"why-doesn-t-benchmark-rank-match-real-usage","title":"Rank vs Usage"},{"_key":"some-models-are-interchangeable-some-aren-t","title":"Interchangeable Models"},{"_key":"so-which-should-you-use","title":"Which to Use"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b8","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1","text":"Google's Nano Banana model family has been at the frontier of image generation. The three frontier Nano Banana models are all built for a different job. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2","text":"Nano Banana Pro","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3","text":" is the one for polished commercial work that needs consistent branding and readable text. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4","text":"Nano Banana 2","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5","text":" is faster and leans cinematic. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6","text":"Nano Banana 2 Lite","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b7","text":" is for cheap, quick iteration, usually under ten seconds a go.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b10","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b9","text":"At Melius we route across every major image and video model rather than betting on one. That gives us a view most people don't have. We can see which model someone picks, what they make with it, how long they wait, and how the choice changes with the job. Here is what our generation data says about the Nano Banana family, and where the real usage parts ways with the leaderboards.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b12","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b11","text":"What are the Nano Banana models?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-are-the-nano-banana-models"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b14","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b13","text":"There are three models in the family, and each one trades speed for quality differently.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b17","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b15","text":"Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image) ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b16","text":"is a reasoning model. It works through the image before rendering, so it handles complex compositions, keeps text readable, and holds branding and characters steady across a shot. That thinking time makes it the slowest of the three.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b20","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b18","text":"Nano Banana 2 (Gemini 3.1 Flash Image) ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b19","text":"is the middle option. It's quick and flexible, and it covers most creative work well.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b23","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b21","text":"Nano Banana 2 Lite (Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite Image) ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b22","text":"is built for speed. Use it for cheap, throwaway iterations, not final work.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b24","rows":[{"_key":"b25","cells":[{"_key":"b26","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b28","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b27","text":"Model","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b29","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b31","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b30","text":"Best for","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b32","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b34","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b33","text":"Relative speed","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b35","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b37","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b36","text":"Signature use","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b38","cells":[{"_key":"b39","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b41","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b40","text":"Nano Banana Pro","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b42","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b44","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b43","text":"Polish & brand fidelity","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b45","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b47","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b46","text":"Slowest","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b48","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b50","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b49","text":"Campaigns, product & food shots, in-image text","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b51","cells":[{"_key":"b52","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b54","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b53","text":"Nano Banana 2","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b55","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b57","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b56","text":"Creative exploration","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b58","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b60","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b59","text":"Fast","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b61","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b63","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b62","text":"Cinematic frames, concept art, characters","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b64","cells":[{"_key":"b65","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b67","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b66","text":"Nano Banana 2 Lite","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b68","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b70","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b69","text":"Quick iteration","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b71","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b73","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b72","text":"Fastest","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b74","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b76","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b75","text":"Rapid prototyping tests","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b78","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b77","text":"How fast is each model?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"how-fast-is-each-model"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b80","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b79","text":"The speed differences track the lineup almost exactly.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"barChart","_key":"b81","title":"Generation latency by model (seconds)","caption":"End-to-end wall-clock time across finished jobs on Melius. Lower is faster.","unit":"s","baseline":0,"series":["Average","Median"],"categories":[{"label":"Nano Banana 2 Lite","values":[9.7,9]},{"label":"Nano Banana 2","values":[29.7,21.5]},{"label":"Nano Banana Pro","values":[38,28.8]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b83","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b82","text":"Lite is much faster, roughly three to four times quicker than the others. Pro is the slowest on average, which is what you'd expect from a reasoning model. Look at the medians, though, and Pro (28.8s) and Nano Banana 2 (21.5s) aren't far apart. The difference is in the tail. Pro has more very slow jobs, and those tend to be the complex compositions where it spends longer working through the image.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b85","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b84","text":"Two caveats. These are end-to-end times that include any queue wait, not pure model inference. And Lite's sample is small, only 238 jobs, so treat its numbers as rough.","marks":["em"]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b87","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b86","text":"What do people actually build with each?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-do-people-actually-build-with-each"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b89","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b88","text":"Latency tells you what a model can do quickly but the prompts tell you what people actually reach for it to do, and here the three variants split apart more than we expected.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b92","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b90","text":"Nano Banana Pro ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b91","text":"handles the commercial work. Its prompts read like production briefs: long, style-locked instructions for campaigns, ads, fashion editorials, and product shots. Food and drink photography shows up far more here than on any other model, around 12.6% of Pro's prompts against 5% or less elsewhere.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b95","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b93","text":"Nano Banana 2 ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b94","text":"leans creative. It gets nearly double the cinematic, film-style prompts that Pro does, about 19.5% against 9.7%, with people calling out lenses, camera angles, and mood, or building out characters and worlds.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b98","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b96","text":"Nano Banana 2 Lite ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b97","text":"gets the least use, mostly quick portrait and landscape tests. It's the pass people make before committing a real job to Pro.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"imageCompare","_key":"b99","caption":"The same prompt run through all three models, a travel flat-lay: â€œa passport, film camera, sunglasses, coins and a boarding pass reading â€˜JFK to LHRâ€™, â€˜GATE 22â€™, seat â€˜14Aâ€™ arranged on a wooden table, top-down, natural light.â€ Look at the composition and the small text on the boarding pass. Pro keeps the layout tidy and the type readable. Nano Banana 2 stays close. Lite gets looser, with softer text and a messier arrangement.","images":[{"label":"Nano Banana Pro","src":"/images/blog/nano-banana/pro.jpg","alt":"Travel flat-lay generated by Nano Banana Pro: passport, film camera, boarding pass reading JFK to LHR, GATE 22, seat 14A, sunglasses and coins on a wooden table","aspectRatio":"3 / 2"},{"label":"Nano Banana 2","src":"/images/blog/nano-banana/nb2.jpg","alt":"Travel flat-lay generated by Nano Banana 2: passport, Fujifilm camera, boarding pass, compass and luggage tag on a wooden table","aspectRatio":"3 / 2"},{"label":"Nano Banana 2 Lite","src":"/images/blog/nano-banana/lite.png","alt":"Travel flat-lay generated by Nano Banana 2 Lite: passport, camera, phone, boarding pass and sunglasses on a wooden table","aspectRatio":"3 / 2"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b101","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b100","text":"How do they score on benchmarks?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"how-do-they-score-on-benchmarks"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b103","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b102","text":"Our data shows how people use these models. Public benchmarks show how the general public perceives the quality of these models in blind head-to-head voting. On text-to-image, the order inside the family is a bit surprising.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"barChart","_key":"b104","title":"Blind text-to-image preference (Elo)","caption":"Higher means more preferred in blind head-to-head voting. The axis starts at 1200 so the gaps are easier to see. These boards move constantly, so read it as a snapshot.","unit":"","baseline":1200,"series":["Text-to-image Elo"],"categories":[{"label":"Nano Banana 2","values":[1270]},{"label":"Nano Banana 2 Lite","values":[1251]},{"label":"Nano Banana Pro","values":[1238]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b106","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b105","text":"Editing flips the order. On single-image edits Pro moves to the front of the family, around 1385 to 1388, ahead of Nano Banana 2, with Lite lower at about 1308. That fits. Editing means reading and changing an existing image, which is where Pro's reasoning and consistency actually pay off.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b108","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b107","text":"Why doesn't benchmark rank match real usage?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"why-doesn-t-benchmark-rank-match-real-usage"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b110","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b109","text":"The interesting part is the mismatch. In blind text-to-image voting, both Nano Banana 2 and even Lite, the cheapest and fastest model, score higher than Pro. On Melius, though, Pro gets used about five times as much as Nano Banana 2. The model people prefer in a vote isn't the model they run.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b112","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b111","text":"A blind vote rewards whatever image looks best on its own. Real work asks for more than that since consistency is key across a whole campaign, text you can read, 4K output, and a model that can take a full style guide as reference and follow it. That's what Nano Banana Pro is built for, and it's the same place the editing benchmarks put it ahead.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b114","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b113","text":"Some models are interchangeable, some aren't","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"some-models-are-interchangeable-some-aren-t"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b116","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b115","text":"We compared Nano Banana Pro with another leading commercial model, and the usage looked almost identical. Both sat around 56% product and e-commerce work and about 16% portraits. That isn't a coincidence. People treat the two as interchangeable and run the same prompt through both to compare. For commercial users they're two tools that do the same job, which is the whole argument for routing across providers.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b118","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b117","text":"Other models look nothing like this. Nano Banana is mostly commercial work, but some models lean toward portraits and people (around 30%) and cinematic or video work (around 25%). They also carry a small adult tail, about 2.6%, that barely registers on Nano Banana, and their prompts run far more international. Same platform, very different crowds.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b120","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b119","text":"So which should you use?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"so-which-should-you-use"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b122","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b121","text":"Put simply:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b125","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b123","text":"Brand campaign, product shots, or anything with text in the frame? ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b124","text":"Use Nano Banana Pro, and try the same prompt on another commercial model too. Your peers already do.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b128","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b126","text":"Selling food or drink? ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b127","text":"Pro again. It does unusually well on this.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b131","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b129","text":"After a cinematic frame, concept art, or a character sheet? ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b130","text":"Nano Banana 2, and it comes back faster.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b134","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b132","text":"Just testing an idea? ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b133","text":"Nano Banana 2 Lite, usually under ten seconds a go.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b137","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b135","text":"Making entertainment or consumer content for a global audience? ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b136","text":"Some of the other models on the platform fit that better.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b145","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b139","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false},{"_type":"link","_key":"b142","href":"/blog/seedance-2-5-anticipation","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b138","text":"None of these is the best image model in the abstract. There's just the model that fits the shot in front of you. That's why Melius runs ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b140","text":"every model under one subscription","marks":["b139"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b141","text":", so you can pick per job instead of committing to one. When the shot needs to move, the same logic carries over to video, where ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b143","text":"Seedance","marks":["b142"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b144","text":" is one of the most-used models on the platform.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b150","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b147","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b146","text":"Want to see how your own generations break down by model? ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b148","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b147"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b149","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b152","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b151","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b153","items":"$40:props:post:faq"}]}}]
41:["$","$L3f","post-text-to-speech-voiceover",{"post":{"_key":"post-text-to-speech-voiceover","slug":"text-to-speech-voiceover","category":"guides","title":"How to turn a script into a natural voiceover on Melius","isoDate":"2026-09-16","date":"September 16, 2026","readTime":"6 Min Read","excerpt":"Text to speech on Melius: turn a written script into a voiceover, direct the delivery, compare takes and balance the audio in your video. Here is what each control does.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/text-to-speech-voiceover/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Melius Team"}],"faq":[{"question":"Can Melius turn written text into speech?","answer":"Yes. Audio nodes support text-to-speech models, so you can generate a spoken recording from a script and use it alongside your other creative assets."},{"question":"Can I control the emotion in a voiceover?","answer":"You can steer expressive delivery using the settings and instructions supported by the selected model. The controls differ between models, and the result still needs a listen before it goes into the final cut."},{"question":"Can I change the voiceover volume?","answer":"Yes. The multi-track editor has clip volume controls for balancing the generated voice against music and other audio. That changes its level in the mix, not the original performance."},{"question":"Is voice selection the same as pitch control?","answer":"No. Selecting a voice changes the starting voice; pitch shifting changes the pitch of a recording. Don't treat one as evidence that the other is available."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"a-natural-voiceover-starts-with-the-read","title":"A natural voiceover starts with the read"},{"_key":"what-to-know-before-you-generate","title":"What to know before you generate"},{"_key":"what-actually-changes-the-sound","title":"What actually changes the sound"},{"_key":"building-the-voiceover-step-by-step","title":"Building the voiceover, step by step"},{"_key":"why-this-belongs-on-the-canvas","title":"Why this belongs on the canvas"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b6128","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6127","text":"A natural voiceover starts with the read","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"a-natural-voiceover-starts-with-the-read"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6130","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6129","text":"Start with how the line should land, because a voice that sounds human can still sound completely wrong for the work. A product explanation needs someone who sounds like they understand the product. A campaign film needs a performance. A tutorial needs a voice that doesn't turn every instruction into a sales pitch. Those are different reads, even when the words are identical.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6132","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6131","text":"On Melius, you turn a written script into speech on an audio node, choose the model and voice, and adjust the delivery before putting the result beside the picture. The script, the generated takes and the rest of the campaign can live on the same canvas. You're not downloading a voiceover from one tool to find out in another that the last sentence doesn't fit.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6134","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6133","text":"The useful distinction is between generating the performance and mixing the recording. Emotion belongs to the first. Volume in the finished video belongs to the second. Treating them as the same control is how a quiet read becomes a loud quiet read instead of a more confident one.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6136","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6135","text":"What to know before you generate","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-to-know-before-you-generate"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6139","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6137","text":"Write for someone speaking.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6138","text":" A sentence that reads well on a landing page can be hard to follow aloud. Shorten the clauses before trying to fix the voice.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6142","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6140","text":"Choose the voice before refining the delivery.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6141","text":" A naturally restrained voice and an energetic one won't respond to the same direction in the same way.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6145","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6143","text":"Controls depend on the model.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6144","text":" Melius carries several speech models, not one universal set of voice settings.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6148","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6146","text":"Judge the voice against the picture.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6147","text":" A take that sounds right alone may rush the reveal or leave the closing frame waiting.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6150","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6149","text":"What actually changes the sound","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-actually-changes-the-sound"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6152","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6151","text":"The voice carries the starting point","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6154","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6153","text":"Voice selection is the first decision, not the finishing touch. Listen for the register, texture and pace that suit the piece before you spend time adjusting an unsuitable voice. If the brand needs something grounded and conversational, start there instead of trying to make an announcer sound as though they're talking across a table.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6159","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b6156","href":"https://docs.melius.com/models/audio","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6155","text":"Melius includes speech models from ElevenLabs, Google, MiniMax and other providers. The ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6157","text":"audio model guide","marks":["b6156"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6158","text":" lists the available families. The point of having several is that you can try the same script against different approaches without moving the whole project.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6161","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6160","text":"Emotion is a performance instruction","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6163","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6162","text":"A line can be reassuring without being slow, excited without being shouted, and serious without sounding flat. Give the model something specific to perform rather than asking it to make the result more natural.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6169","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6164","text":"Supported models accept expressive direction. Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS, for example, supports inline instructions and tags such as ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6165","text":"[whispering]","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6166","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6167","text":"[laughing]","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6168","text":". ElevenLabs models expose delivery settings that vary by model, including stability, style and pacing. These are ways to steer a take, not guarantees that every sentence will land exactly as intended.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6171","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6170","text":"Work on a short passage first. If the opening is supposed to sound like a recommendation from a friend, settle that read before generating the rest of the script. Otherwise you're reviewing a long recording whose first decision was already wrong.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6173","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6172","text":"Volume belongs in the mix","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6175","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6174","text":"Once the read works, bring it into the multi-track editor with the video and music. Melius has clip volume controls, so you can balance the voice against the rest of the soundtrack without asking the speech model to perform again.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6177","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6176","text":"That separation matters. If the music covers the last word of each sentence, the problem isn't the script or the voice. Lower the music. If the speaker sounds too enthusiastic, changing the level won't fix the performance. Go back to the audio node and change the delivery.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6179","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6178","text":"Pitch is a separate requirement","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6181","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6180","text":"Choosing a lower-register voice is not the same as shifting the pitch of an existing recording. Neither is changing speaking speed. If the job requires an exact pitch adjustment, treat that as a separate audio-processing requirement; the Melius controls described here don't establish a dedicated pitch-shifting feature.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6183","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6182","text":"It's a distinction worth making before a workflow becomes a promise to a client. Voice choice and expressive direction give you room to shape the sound, but they aren't substitutes for a specified pitch control.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6185","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6184","text":"Building the voiceover, step by step","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"building-the-voiceover-step-by-step"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6188","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6186","text":"Put the spoken script on an audio node.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6187","text":" Use the words you want read, with punctuation that reflects the pauses. Choose a text-to-speech model and a voice.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6191","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6189","text":"Generate a short test.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6190","text":" Start with the opening and the most awkward line, not the whole script. Names, abbreviations and long product descriptions are worth hearing early.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6194","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6192","text":"Refine the delivery.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6193","text":" Adjust the settings or expressive instructions supported by that model. Change one thing at a time so you know what improved the take.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6197","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6195","text":"Generate the full read and place it in the cut.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6196","text":" Check the timing against the visuals, especially reveals, transitions and the closing frame.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6200","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6198","text":"Balance the soundtrack.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6199","text":" Adjust clip volumes in the editor, listen to the complete sequence, and download the finished result when it works.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6202","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6201","text":"Why this belongs on the canvas","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"why-this-belongs-on-the-canvas"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6204","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6203","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work, built around a canvas where the inputs and outputs remain visible. For voiceover work, the useful part is that the script isn't detached from the thing it describes. The product images, the video and the read belong to one piece of work, so a change to the wording doesn't need to become a hunt through exported files.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6212","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b6206","href":"/blog/static-ad-from-style-reference","isNewTab":false},{"_type":"link","_key":"b6209","href":"/blog/brief-to-execution-workflow","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6205","text":"The same principle sits behind ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6207","text":"building a static ad from a style reference","marks":["b6206"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6208","text":": make the direction explicit, keep the steps open, and correct the part that missed. For the larger campaign, see the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6210","text":"Brief-to-Execution workflow","marks":["b6209"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6211","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6214","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6213","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b6215","items":"$41:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6220","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b6217","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6216","text":"Start with the first two sentences of a script. Get the read right on ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6218","text":"Melius","marks":["b6217"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6219","text":", then build the rest around it.","marks":[]}]}]}}]
